//! FilmCraft on phones: the engine as a native library for the Android app in `android/`, with
//! bindings generated by [UniFFI](https://mozilla.github.io/uniffi-rs).
//!
//! The phone UI is one more frontend next to the desktop app, the CLI/MCP server and the web
//! build. It shows a simple timeline laid over the engine's tracks ([`model`]): a gapless main
//! track, overlay lanes above it and audio lanes below. Every edit is one engine command or one
//! group of them, so each is one undo step ([`edits`], [`text`]). Pictures and sound come from a
//! [`render::Renderer`], a snapshot of the project that draws without holding the session, so the
//! app can play, scrub and draw thumbnails on several threads while it edits.
//!
//! Time crosses the bridge as engine ticks (`filmcraft_time::Tick`, 254 016 000 000 per second),
//! never as floating-point seconds, so edits stay frame-exact.
//!
//! Threading: every method may be called from any thread; the session lock is held for the
//! duration of a call, so the UI calls them off its main thread.
#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
#![deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::unimplemented, clippy::todo, clippy::unreachable)]

